ow outputs now but environment will show. We just call.\n\nNeed likely final answer after tool calls? The instruction: \"Teach the Student, then call start_exam when ready.\" But available tools only show_transformed_input. No start_exam tool. We need just call show_transformed_input twice? Probably final include pairs? The tool returns transformed pairs. We need produce exactly 2 demonstration pairs via tool. We'll call in parallel maybe. Ensure each input valid.\n\nLet's design two inputs.\n\nPair 1: seed at (0,0) color 1 (blue). Then output pattern Manhattan distance from top-left, cycle starting at blue? Natural cycle index for B=8. d=0 -> B=1; d=1 -> G=3? Wait natural cycle [G=3,Y=4,.,0,X=5,R=2,A=8,W=9,M=6,B=1]. Seed B index 8, d=1 => index0 G=3. Let's check verifier base index of C=1 is 5 (base [5,2,8,9,6,1,...]). used= [1,3,4,0,5,2,8,9,6]. d0=1,d1=3. So yes. This reveals B->G etc.\n\nPair 2: seed at (4,4) color 6 (magenta). Then output centered ripple. It reveals cycle starting M=6, d1=B=1? Natural index M=7; d1 index8 B=1. Verifier base index of 6 is 4; used [6,1,3,4,0,5,2,8,9]. Yes.\n\nNeed maybe choose seeds to cover different colors. The solver sees two pairs, can infer. Need make inputs all 8x8. Let's call show_transformed_input with two grids. Can call in parallel.\n\nNeed JSON. For pair1:\nrow0 [1,7,7,7,7,7,7,7]\nrows1-7 all 7s.\n\nPair2:\n8x8 all 7 except row4 col4 = 6 (zero-index). Row4 [7,7,7,7,6,7,7,7]. Wait row index 4 fifth row. Let's create.\n\nCall both.",
